course: dictionary
lesson: 11509
title: Airborne
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Airborne» means moving or carried through the air. The word has two parts: air, and borne, which means carried. So something airborne is held up by the air, not resting on the ground.
explain: «The dandelion seeds were airborne on the windy hill.» The seeds are not walking or rolling. The wind carries them. The clues are windy and seeds, so airborne must mean carried through the air. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «The seeds were carried through the air» still makes sense.
explain: Airborne can also mean off the ground and flying. «The plane became airborne at six o'clock.» A plane that is airborne has left the runway and is in the sky. Clue words like plane, runway and sky help you decide which meaning fits.
fact: Airborne means moving or carried through the air.
fact: «Airborne» can also mean off the ground and flying, as in «The plane is airborne.»
fact: Airborne seeds, like dandelion and sycamore seeds, travel on the wind.
fact: Some germs travel in tiny drops in the air, so «airborne germs» can spread when someone coughs or sneezes.
fact: In the army, «airborne troops» are soldiers trained to arrive by parachute or aircraft.
exercise: «The seeds were airborne on the windy hill.» What does airborne mean here? | Tall and green | *Carried through the air | Very heavy | Stuck in the mud
exercise: «The plane became airborne after a long run down the runway.» What does airborne mean? | Parked at the airport | Full of passengers | *Off the ground and flying | Lost in fog
exercise: «The soldiers were trained as airborne troops.» What are airborne troops? | *Soldiers trained to arrive by parachute or aircraft | Soldiers who sleep all day | Soldiers who sail boats | Soldiers who dig tunnels
test: «Tiny germs can be airborne when someone sneezes.» What does airborne suggest? | The germs stay on the table | The germs are very large and heavy | *The germs travel through the air in tiny drops | The germs are a kind of food
test: Ella says airborne means underwater. Why is she wrong? | Airborne means sinking slowly | *Airborne means in the air, the opposite of underwater | Airborne means underwater in science | Airborne means very deep under the sea
exam: Jayden reads, «The footballer was airborne for a second before he landed.» What does airborne mean? | *Off the ground, flying through the air | Running very fast along the ground | Sitting on the grass | Hurt and unable to play
